# XSH fputs()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.fputs.001
anchor     functions/fputs.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/fputs.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       On a stream opened "w", fputs("hello") and then fputs("") each
           return a non-negative value, and after fclose() the file holds
           exactly the 5 bytes "hello" (no null byte).
note       Which non-negative value is open (APPLICATION USAGE lists a
           constant, the last byte and the byte count); variants
           fputs.returns_count and fputs.returns_last.
test       t/001-writes.c

assertion  XSH.fputs.002
anchor     functions/fputs.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     functions/fputc.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
says       On an unbuffered stream opened "w" whose descriptor was closed,
           fputs("ab") returns EOF, sets errno to EBADF and sets the
           stream's error indicator.
note       Where setvbuf() refuses _IONBF, the test writes until a call
           fails; if none does within 4 MiB the result is UNRESOLVED.
test       t/002-ebadf.c

assertion  XSH.fputs.003
anchor     functions/fputs.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       On a stream opened "r+" on a file whose modification time is set
           to 2001-09-09, after fputs("xy") and a successful fflush(),
           fstat() shows a later st_mtim.
note       As for XSH.fputc.005 (the change time is not checked).
test       t/003-mtime.c
